    <value>A rented computer for this run already exists. Open the Cloud page and delete it, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_permission" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your Google account is not allowed to do this, or its sign-in has expired. Sign in again from Settings, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_org_policy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your organization blocks this action in the project. Ask your Google Cloud administrator to allow it, or choose a different project in Settings.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_network" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Google Cloud could not be reached. Check your internet connection, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_vm_unhealthy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The rented computer stopped or was lost during the run. Start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_lifecycle_unverified" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your results were saved, but we could not confirm that the rented computer has shut down, so it may still be billing. Open the Cloud page and delete it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_cancel_failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We could not delete the rented computer while cancelling. Open the Cloud page and delete it so it stops billing.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_missing" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We could not read your input file. Choose the file again, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_no_worker_image" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This copy of the app does not include the analysis software it sends to the rented computer, so it cannot run an analysis yet. Check the app's download page for a newer version, install it, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_worker_image_refused" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This app does not recognise the analysis software your computer is set to use, so it will not send it to the rented computer. Check the app's download page for a newer version of the app, install it, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_result_timeout" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The rented computer did not finish in time, so we shut it down. Start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_vm_end_unconfirmed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The run stopped, but we could not confirm that the rented computer has shut down, so it may still be billing. Open the Cloud page and delete it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_gpu_not_visible" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The rented computer started without a working graphics card, so the analysis could not begin. Start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_image_pull_failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The rented computer could not download the analysis software. Start the run again in a few minutes.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_manifest_invalid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The rented computer could not read the instructions for this run. Choose Save diagnostics in Settings and send the file to support.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_worker_crashed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The analysis program on the rented computer stopped unexpectedly. Choose Save diagnostics in Settings and send the file to support.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_model_needs_hopper" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This model needs a very large graphics card that you did not choose and that is hard to get. Choose the default model, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_model_oom" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The stretch of sequence being analysed at once is too big for this graphics card's memory. Lower the context length in the run options, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_batch_limit_exceeded" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This batch of files is larger than the limit that protects you from a surprise bill. Split it into smaller batches, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_invalid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Something is wrong with your sequence file, so the analysis could not start. Check the file, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_worker_version_mismatch" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your app and the analysis software on the rented computer are different versions. Check the app's download page for a newer version, install it, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_output_folder_unusable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We could not use your output folder, so nothing was started and nothing was billed. Choose a different output folder, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_cloud_not_connected" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Running in the cloud is not connected in this version of the app yet, so nothing was sent to Google and nothing was billed. Check the app's download page for a newer version, install it, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_worker_failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The analysis did not finish on the rented computer. Choose Save diagnostics in Settings and send the file to support.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_download_failed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We could not save your results to your computer, but they are still stored in your Google Cloud project. Free up space in your output folder, then download the results again from the Runs page.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_download_corrupt" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A result file arrived damaged, so we did not keep it. The original is still stored in your Google Cloud project. Download the results again from the Runs page.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_invalid_character" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your sequence file contains a character that is not a DNA letter (A, C, G or T). Open the file, remove or correct that character, then choose the file again and start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_ambiguity_refused" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your sequence file contains ambiguous base codes (such as N), and this run is set to refuse them. In the run options, set ambiguous bases to Keep or Mask, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_rna" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your sequence file contains the letter U, which means it is RNA. In the run options, turn on treating the input as RNA, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_not_utf8" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your sequence file was not saved as UTF-8 text, so some characters could not be read. Open the file in a text editor, save it again with UTF-8 encoding, then choose the file again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_empty" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We found no sequence in your file. Check that it is a FASTA or GenBank file that contains at least one sequence, then choose the file again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_input_too_long" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your sequence file is longer than one run can analyze. Split it into smaller files, choose one of them, then start the run again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="RunError_other" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Something went wrong while running in the cloud. Choose Save diagnostics in Settings and send the file to support.</value>
  </data>
